course: dictionary
lesson: 711
title: Barely: just, or hardly at all
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Barely» means only just, or hardly at all. «I barely caught the bus» means I got on with almost no time to spare. Try the swap: «I almost missed the bus» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: «She barely ate» means she ate very little. Swap in «hardly at all» and the sentence still makes sense: she hardly ate at all. The clues are the words around barely, not a dictionary.
explain: Barely can also show a very short time. «We had barely sat down when the phone rang» means we had only just sat down before the phone rang.
fact: «Barely» is an adverb. It tells you more about a verb, an adjective or another adverb, such as how much or how little.
fact: «Barely» means only just, or hardly at all.
fact: «Barely» can also mean only a very short time before, as in «We had barely sat down when the phone rang».
fact: Barely and bare sound similar, but they are different words. «Bare» means without clothes or covering.
fact: A good check is to swap in «only just» or «hardly at all» and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «I barely caught the bus.» What does barely mean here? | Very easily | Not at all | *Only just | Quickly and happily
exercise: «Pigs barely sweat at all, so they roll in mud to keep cool.» What does barely mean here? | Only after lunch | Loudly | *Hardly at all | Very much
exercise: «We had barely sat down when the phone rang.» What does barely tell us about the time? | A long time after | We were still standing up | *Only a very short time before | The phone was broken
test: «The first month she barely spoke in class.» What does barely mean? | Without clothes | *Hardly at all | Every single day | Very loudly
test: «The plant barely notices.» What does this tell us about the plant? | *It hardly notices at all | It notices very loudly | It has no leaves | It notices every bee
exam: «The baby tooth barely hurts.» Which swap keeps the same meaning? | Hurts in the morning | Very hurts | *Hardly hurts | Hurts loudly
